>I am a beginner and need some advice on stockpiling. I have collected 
>enough items now, and before I get burdened, I think it is time to 
>decide on what to leave behind (for possible future use) and what to 
>take along to aid survival.
>
>What could happen to a stockpile and in which places is it safest to 
>leave one? Can I assume, that a stockpile left in a small room which I 
>have cleansed from monsters (the surroundings aswell) and closed/blocked 
>all doors will remain fairly safe for a long time or at least until I 
>return, whenever that should be necessary? Can I lock a chest and assume 
>that it will not be tampered with by monsters? What are other risks?
>What tips can you give me on stockpiling?

Put everything into a container...ice chest, normal chest, box, or bag.
Keeps it together, and prevents item-hungry spawns from picking it up and
using it on you (see: Uruk-Hai swarms).

If you are not on the level where your stash is located, then nothing will
ever happen to it. Levels where you are not physically present are frozen
in the state where you left them. Time still passes (relevant for corpses,
which will decay in your absence), but nothing actually occurs until you
get back to that level. So, put your stash near the down stairs, and it
will be essentially immune from any kind of tampering. If you wish to be
paranoid, you can always use a wand of fire/lightning and burn the E word
into the ground underneath the stash...that will keep most critters away
from it.



